WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-First of all, happy birthday!

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's your birthday.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:03.803 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And...
-Oh, wow! 25 again.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
-25 again.
-Yeah.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And not only are you spending
your birthday with us,

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.808 size:75% position:38%
but then, of course,
you're going to go

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.111
and you're going to do your show
live at 10:00 tonight...

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
-...for two hours.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.547 size:84% position:42%
Is that the perfect way
to spend a birthday,

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.916
surrounded by a panel of people
talking about what happens

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.053
in the news every day?
-As opposed to with Seth Meyers?

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, it is.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
Actually, I -- I, well --
thank you.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I love what I do.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great!
-It's a great way to spend

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.461
my birthday, and what we're
covering now is so important.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.730
So I can't imagine
any other thing, any other way,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.233
except with maybe with my
partner or with my family.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm so --
I think you do a great job.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-And I also want to just

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.740 line:92%
speak to the level of difficulty

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
anyone who has to manage
a panel has

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.979
versus what I get to do
which is I have you here,

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:46.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're the person
I have to talk to.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Right.
-It's very easy.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to finish talking
to you and then say,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
"And now you hate Don Lemon."
So...

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Or someone is yelling at you.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Behind you or in

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.523 line:92%
a satellite box or in your ear.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't say that,
or get to the break."

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because sometimes
they're not even there.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-How much --

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.697
I guess my question is how
much of it is that organizing

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your head where
you're going go next

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:09.569
and how you keep it all in
the -- juggling in the air?

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.472
-I try to be fair and not let
people talk over each other

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
or let other people talk
too much.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I want it to be organic,
a conversation.

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.446 size:84% position:42%
I try not to, you know,
ask canned questions.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.815
But it's tough. Sometimes
I forget people's names.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.982
-Uh-huh.
-And I have to look at my card,

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:25.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
the blue card and go, "Wait
a minute, um -- wait a minute.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
That's Chris and not Rob."

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Sometimes I get it wrong.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:31.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you do a lot of like,
"Hey, buddy, what about you?"

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.928
-Yes, so it is always, you know,
"And what do you think?"

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.430
-Yeah, right.
-But sometimes it's really easy

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.300
because all you have to do
is say, you know, "Seth?"

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.168
-Right.
-And then just let someone talk.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.336 line:92%
-Well, that's the other thing.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say everyone
on those panels,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:47.740
they're basically wind-up toys
who are ready to go if you --

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
If you turn it over to them,

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not -- I've never seen
anyone on a panel say,

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.379
"You know what, Don? I got
nothing to say about this."

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.982
-And when we do, we mark it,
because every once in a while,

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
we stump people and they say,
"You know what,

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really don't have an answer
to that."

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:02.922
-Now, one thing that we've
been talking about on this show

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
is it's this crazy thing
that happens now,

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:07.260
which Donald Trump will suggest
something so far afield

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.063
of conventional wisdom, and yet,
because he's the president

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:13.399
and because it's the news, you
actually have to have a panel

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
and talk about this stuff.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like we should have a ratings
system for movies?

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. For movies.
So he says that and then --

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then you have to go --

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:22.976 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and, like, say, like,

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:28.214
"What do you have to say about
this totally nonsensical thing?"

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:28.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talked about it,
and I saw it.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-With Wolf Blitzer.

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.785 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, it's crazy.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.523 line:92%
And I try not to engage in that,

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.425
and I will say, you know,
I do give a point of view

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
on my show,
which is interesting,

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.328
I think people find interesting
for CNN.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.964
I do give a point of view,
and I'll say that's ridiculous.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, we can be fair,

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:49.235
we can be open minded,
but we don't have to be stupid.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:54.474
But, seriously.
-Yeah, I think that's very fair.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One issue is arming teachers.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.444
-And, you know, I come from
a long line of teachers,

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:01.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
and none of them want to be
armed in school.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.982
-Yeah.
-Do we want security in school?

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.485
Absolutely. But do -- you know,
do you want your teacher,

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you want Coach Edwards
to be armed?

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I don't think so.

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.789 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-My mom was a teacher,

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:11.524 line:92%
and if she ever had a gun,

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
so many things would have
had to go wrong.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You might not be here.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.929 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

